---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { MUNICIPAL_ELECTION_DATES_2026 } from '../data/municipal';
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Vote - Provincial & Municipal Elections - Autario Votes"
  description="Comprehensive voting guides for both Ontario Provincial Elections (Elections Ontario) and Simcoe County Municipal Elections (Municipal Elections Act)."
>
  <div class="container page-content">
    <!-- ========================================== -->
    <!-- 1. MUNICIPAL HOW TO VOTE (MUNICIPAL ACT)  -->
    <!-- ========================================== -->
    <div class="municipal-only">
      <div class="header-section">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-mun">Simcoe County Local Government</span>
        <h1>How to Vote in Simcoe County Municipal Elections</h1>
        <p class="intro">
          Municipal elections in Ontario are administered by each local municipality under the <strong>Municipal Elections Act, 1996</strong>. The next municipal general election is on <strong>Monday, October 26, 2026</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Municipal Eligibility -->
      <section class="guide-card card-mun-border">
        <div class="card-icon">🏡</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>1. Who Can Vote in Municipal Elections?</h2>
          <p>Under Section 17 of the <em>Municipal Elections Act</em>, a person is entitled to vote in a municipal election if they are:</p>
          <ul class="checklist check-mun">
            <li><strong>At least 18 years of age</strong> on Election Day;</li>
            <li>A <strong>Canadian citizen</strong>; and</li>
            <li>Either a <strong>resident</strong> of the municipality, or the <strong>owner or tenant of land</strong> in the municipality, or the <strong>spouse of such an owner or tenant</strong>.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="cottager-callout">
            <h3>🏖️ Cottagers & Seasonal Property Owners Can Vote!</h3>
            <p>
              Unlike provincial elections, <strong>non-resident property owners</strong> (such as seasonal cottagers across Georgian Bay, Lake Simcoe, and rural townships) are legally entitled to vote in the municipality where their property is located! 
            </p>
            <p>
              If you live in Toronto or York Region but own a cottage in Wasaga Beach, Collingwood, Oro-Medonte, Severn, Ramara, or Tiny, you can vote in <strong>both</strong> your home city's municipal election AND your cottage municipality's election.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What is on the Municipal Ballot? -->
      <section class="guide-card card-mun-border">
        <div class="card-icon">🗳️</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>2. What Offices Are on the Municipal Ballot?</h2>
          <p>When you cast your ballot in a Simcoe County municipal election, you vote for key municipal and education offices:</p>

          <div class="ballot-roles-grid">
            <div class="ballot-role-card">
              <span class="role-badge-chip">Head of Council</span>
              <h3>1. Mayor</h3>
              <p>Contested at-large by voters across the municipality to serve as head of council and chief executive officer.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ballot-role-card">
              <span class="role-badge-chip">County Representative</span>
              <h3>2. Deputy Mayor</h3>
              <p>Contested at-large to serve as Deputy Head of Council and represent the town/township at County of Simcoe Council.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ballot-role-card">
              <span class="role-badge-chip">Local Neighbourhood Voice</span>
              <h3>3. Ward Councillor</h3>
              <p>Contested by voters within your specific ward (or at-large in smaller townships) to represent neighbourhood infrastructure, planning, and bylaws.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ballot-role-card">
              <span class="role-badge-chip">Education Trustee</span>
              <h3>4. School Board Trustee</h3>
              <p>Contested by school board supporters to govern regional education policy and budgets across local schools.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Municipal Registration & VoterLookup.ca -->
      <section class="guide-card card-mun-border">
        <div class="card-icon">📋</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>3. Checking the Municipal Voters' List (VoterLookup.ca)</h2>
          <p>
            The Municipal Property Assessment Corporation (MPAC) compiles property assessment and tenant data to generate the preliminary voters' list for each municipality.
          </p>
          <div class="action-row">
            <a href="https://www.voterlookup.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-secondary">
              Check Your Municipal Registration at VoterLookup.ca ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="note-text">
            <strong>School Board Support Declaration:</strong> In Ontario, your voter registration indicates which school board you support (English Public, English Catholic, French Public, or French Catholic). This determines which school board trustee race appears on your municipal ballot.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Voting Methods by Municipality -->
      <section class="guide-card card-mun-border">
        <div class="card-icon">💻</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>4. Voting Methods Across Simcoe County</h2>
          <p>
            Each municipality determines its authorized voting methods by municipal bylaw under the <em>Municipal Elections Act</em>:
          </p>

          <div class="methods-summary-grid">
            <div class="method-card">
              <h3>🌐 Internet & Telephone Voting</h3>
              <p>
                Used exclusively by the <strong>City of Barrie</strong>, <strong>Innisfil</strong>, <strong>Bradford West Gwillimbury</strong>, <strong>Midland</strong>, <strong>Tiny</strong>, <strong>Tay</strong>, <strong>Clearview</strong>, <strong>Oro-Medonte</strong>, <strong>Springwater</strong>, and <strong>Adjala-Tosorontio</strong>. Voters receive a secure PIN by mail and can cast their ballot online or via telephone 24/7 without paper ballots.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="method-card">
              <h3>🗳️ In-Person Paper Ballots</h3>
              <p>
                The <strong>City of Orillia</strong> conducts its municipal election exclusively via in-person paper ballots counted by ImageCast Precinct optical tabulators (Orillia City Council voted against internet voting due to cybersecurity concerns). The <strong>Township of Essa</strong> also uses traditional in-person paper ballots.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="method-card">
              <h3>🔄 Hybrid Voting (Internet + Paper)</h3>
              <p>
                Municipalities including <strong>Collingwood</strong>, <strong>Wasaga Beach</strong>, <strong>New Tecumseth</strong>, <strong>Penetanguishene</strong>, <strong>Severn</strong>, and <strong>Ramara</strong> offer hybrid models, combining multi-week 24/7 internet voting with in-person paper ballot polling locations and optical tabulators.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="method-card">
              <h3>🏢 Voter Assistance Centres & Kiosks</h3>
              <p>
                Every municipality—including 100% digital jurisdictions like Barrie—sets up physical Voter Assistance Centres at Town Halls, libraries, and community facilities equipped with touchscreens, tablets, accessible peripherals, and staff assistance.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Dates Section -->
      <section class="guide-card card-mun-border">
        <div class="card-icon">📅</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>5. 2026 Municipal Election Dates</h2>
          <div class="dates-mini-grid">
            {MUNICIPAL_ELECTION_DATES_2026.map((d) => (
              <div class="date-chip">
                <strong>{d.title}</strong>
                <span class="d-val">{d.date}</span>
                <span class="d-sub">{d.desc}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ========================================== -->
    <!-- 2. PROVINCIAL HOW TO VOTE (ELECTIONS ON)  -->
    <!-- ========================================== -->
    <div class="provincial-only">
      <div class="header-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Elections Ontario Guide</span>
        <h1>How to Vote in Ontario Provincial Elections</h1>
        <p class="intro">
          Provincial elections in Ontario are administered by <strong>Elections Ontario</strong>, an independent agency of the Legislative Assembly. Learn about eligibility rules, voter registration, approved identification, and your options for casting a ballot.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Eligibility Section -->
      <section class="guide-card">
        <div class="card-icon">👤</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>1. Who Can Vote in Ontario?</h2>
          <p>To be eligible to vote in an Ontario provincial general election or by-election, you must be:</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><strong>At least 18 years of age</strong> on Election Day;</li>
            <li>A <strong>Canadian citizen</strong>; and</li>
            <li>A <strong>resident of Ontario</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="callout-box">
            <p>
              Students attending university or college in Ontario can choose to vote either at their home address or at their student residence address, but not both.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Registration Section -->
      <section class="guide-card">
        <div class="card-icon">📝</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>2. Register to Vote (RegisterToVoteON.ca)</h2>
          <p>
            Elections Ontario maintains the permanent Register of Electors for the province. 
            When you are registered, you will automatically receive a <strong>Voter Information Card (VIC)</strong> in the mail before Election Day detailing your assigned voting location.
          </p>
          <div class="action-row">
            <a href="https://registertovoteon.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">
              Check or Update Registration at RegisterToVoteON.ca ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="note-text">
            <em>Didn't register ahead of time?</em> In Ontario, you can always register in person at your polling station when you go to vote. Just bring acceptable ID proving your name and residential address.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4 Ways to Vote -->
      <section class="guide-card">
        <div class="card-icon">🗳️</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>3. Four Ways to Cast Your Ballot</h2>
          <p>Ontario provides multiple flexible, accessible ways to vote:</p>

          <div class="options-grid">
            <div class="option-box">
              <span class="opt-badge">Option A</span>
              <h3>Vote on Election Day</h3>
              <p>
                Polls are open from <strong>9:00 AM to 9:00 PM Eastern Time</strong>. 
                Cast your ballot in person at your designated neighbourhood polling station as listed on your Voter Information Card.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="option-box">
              <span class="opt-badge">Option B</span>
              <h3>Advance Voting</h3>
              <p>
                Advance voting locations operate across each riding for several consecutive days before Election Day. Any registered voter in the riding may vote at any designated advance voting location.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="option-box">
              <span class="opt-badge">Option C</span>
              <h3>Vote by Mail</h3>
              <p>
                Electors can request a mail-in voting kit online through the Elections Ontario portal once the election writ is issued. Ballots must be received by 8:00 PM on Election Day.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="option-box">
              <span class="opt-badge">Option D</span>
              <h3>Vote at the Returning Office</h3>
              <p>
                Each riding has an official Returning Office open six days a week during an election campaign. You can vote by special ballot in person from the day after the writ is issued until 6:00 PM the evening before Election Day.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Required Identification Section -->
      <section class="guide-card">
        <div class="card-icon">🪪</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>4. Required Identification (ID)</h2>
          <p>
            Under the Ontario <em>Election Act</em>, you must show <strong>one piece of identification that shows both your NAME and current RESIDENTIAL ADDRESS</strong>.
          </p>

          <div class="id-grid">
            <div class="id-group">
              <h3>Accepted Government IDs (One piece required):</h3>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Ontario Driver's Licence</strong> (shows name & residential address)</li>
                <li><strong>Ontario Photo Card</strong> (shows name & residential address)</li>
                <li>Ontario Motor Vehicle Permit (vehicle registration)</li>
                <li>Income Tax Assessment Notice or Canadian Notice of Assessment</li>
                <li>Government of Ontario or Government of Canada benefit statement</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="id-group">
              <h3>Other Accepted Proof of Residence Documents:</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Residential lease, sub-lease, or mortgage agreement</li>
                <li>Utility bill (hydro, gas, water, internet, or cable)</li>
                <li>Bank statement, credit card statement, or credit union document</li>
                <li>Pay stub or employment letter with residential address</li>
                <li>Property tax assessment or bill</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="warning-callout">
            <strong>⚠️ Important Note on Ontario Health Cards:</strong>
            <p>
              An Ontario Health Card does <strong>not</strong> display your residential address. While it proves your identity and photo, you must pair it with a document proving your residential address (such as a utility bill, bank statement, or lease) to cast your ballot.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Official Contacts -->
      <section class="guide-card contact-card">
        <div class="card-icon">📞</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>Official Elections Ontario Inquiries</h2>
          <p>For questions regarding provincial polling locations, returning offices, or special ballots:</p>
          <div class="contacts-list">
            <div class="contact-item">
              <strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.elections.on.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">elections.on.ca ↗</a>
            </div>
            <div class="contact-item">
              <strong>Toll-Free Phone:</strong> 1-888-668-8683 (1-888-ONT-VOTE)
            </div>
            <div class="contact-item">
              <strong>Voter Registry Portal:</strong> <a href="https://registertovoteon.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RegisterToVoteON.ca ↗</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .header-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow-mun {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
    max-width: 850px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .guide-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
  }

  .card-mun-border {
    border-left: 5px solid var(--secondary);
  }

  .card-icon {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .card-body {
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .card-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .card-body p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .checklist li {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.75rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: "✓";
    color: #10b981;
    font-weight: bold;
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }

  .check-mun li::before {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .callout-box {
    background: #f0fdf4;
    border-left: 4px solid #10b981;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 0 0.375rem 0.375rem 0;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .callout-box p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #166534;
  }

  .cottager-callout {
    background: #f0fdfa;
    border: 1px solid #99f6e4;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--secondary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cottager-callout h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--secondary-dark);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cottager-callout p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #134e4a;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cottager-callout p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .ballot-roles-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .ballot-role-card {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .role-badge-chip {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #ccfbf1;
    color: #0f766e;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ballot-role-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .ballot-role-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .methods-summary-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .method-card {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .method-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .method-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .dates-mini-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .date-chip {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .date-chip strong {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .date-chip .d-val {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--secondary-dark);
    margin: 0.25rem 0;
  }

  .date-chip .d-sub {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  .action-row {
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    background: var(--secondary);
    color: white;
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--secondary-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .note-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  .options-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .option-box {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .opt-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #e2e8f0;
    color: #334155;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .option-box h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .option-box p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-light);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .id-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .id-group {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .id-group h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .id-group ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .id-group li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .warning-callout {
    background: #fffbeb;
    border: 1px solid #fde68a;
    border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b;
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .warning-callout strong {
    color: #92400e;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .warning-callout p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #78350f;
  }

  .contact-card {
    background: #f8fafc;
    border-color: #cbd5e1;
  }

  .contacts-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .contact-item {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .guide-card {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }

    .card-icon {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>